    "summary": "Dark Star marathon, tight rhythm section, legendary jam flow",
    "blurb": "The show shines with a multi‑part Dark Star that segues into Attics Of My Life and Sugar Magnolia, plus a high‑energy Not Fade Away chase. Jerry’s tone is razor‑sharp, Phil’s bass locks in, and the drums drive the psychedelic momentum.",
    "review": "June 24, 1970 at the Capitol Theater captured one of the early Dead’s most electrifying nights. From the opening set of folk‑blues numbers the band built into a soaring second set where Dark Star appears three times, weaving through Attics Of My Life, Sugar Magnolia and Saint Stephen before landing on a blistering I Know You Rider. Reviewers repeatedly call Jerry’s guitar tone “perfect” and “break‑neck,” noting his otherworldly vibe throughout the marathon jams. Phil Lesh’s bass is described as “banging away” and locked in with the rhythm section, especially during the Not Fade Away chase and Easy Wind. The twin drummers provide a solid, \"locked\" foundation that fuels the psychedelic flow, while Bob Weir adds his outlaw‑cowboy vocal flair on Me And My Uncle. Even though all available sources are audience recordings, several capture the performance with surprising clarity, making this a must‑listen snapshot of the Dead’s 1970 summer run.",
